                            <comment id="16191210" author="vozerov" created="Wed, 4 Oct 2017 12:59:25 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;In addition, please pay attention that according to JDBC spec, setSchema() should not affect previously created statements. This is not the case for thin driver at the moment. Needs to be fixed.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16191442" author="tledkov-gridgain" created="Wed, 4 Oct 2017 15:34:59 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;What about the caches without specified sql schema. When &lt;tt&gt;cacheName&lt;/tt&gt; is used to create SQL schema? In this case &lt;b&gt;cacheName&lt;/b&gt; isn&apos;t modified.&lt;br/&gt;
e.g.:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;cacheConfiguration.setName(&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;person&quot;&lt;/span&gt;);
...
conn.setSqlSchema(&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;person&quot;&lt;/span&gt;);
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt; fail with error &quot;Failed to set schema for DB connection for thread &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;schema=&amp;quot;PERSON&amp;quot;&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&quot;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Is it OK or incompatible behavior?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
